  "an5.167:0.3": "<p><i>The text to Saṅghādisesa 12, one of the rules in the Vinaya, states: “Let the venerable one admonish the monks in accordance with what is Dhamma, and the monks will admonish the venerable one in accordance with what is Dhamma; for it is thus that the Blessed One’s following is nurtured: through mutual admonition, through mutual rehabilitation.”</i></p><p><i>This sutta discusses the proper way in which an accusation should be handled to be in keeping with this principle.</i></p><p>See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn66'>MN 66</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn70'>MN 70</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.30'>AN 5:30</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.42'>AN 6:42</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.86'>AN 8:103</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp76-89#dhp076'>Dhp 76–77</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp360-382#dhp379'>Dhp 379</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/ud3.3'>Ud 3:3</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/ud4.2'>Ud 4:2</a></p>",
